  "followed": "a take FOLLOWED its previs when cam_follow >= 0.70 (mean correlation of the pan x / pan y / log-zoom paths vs the previs over all 124 f, axes where the previs moves >= 0.02) AND its dominant axis moves in the same direction as the previs. Amplitude is reported, not part of the criterion (overshoot is a finding, not a failure). Words-only twins are scored against the same previs path with the same rule.",
  "w7_dolly_zoom": "w7 counts as followed only if the shot's written decision rule passes: her size within +-10 % of frame 0 AND the background swells >= +30 % on a feature shared with frame 0. The global path cannot express a dolly zoom.",
  "tie": "previs vs words-only per move: |cam_follow(previs take) - cam_follow(words-only twin)| < 0.10 is a TIE; otherwise the higher follow wins. If both fail the followed rule, the move is 'neither' whatever the gap.",
  "counts": "n_previs = production takes that FOLLOWED; n_words = words-only twins that FOLLOWED (same rule, same 8 moves). First takes only (the retry is reported apart, never swapped into n_previs).",
  "overshoot": "cam_amp of the 8 production takes and their median; > 1 = H3 moved more than the previs.",
  "stage": "every previs-vs-words comparison is raw H3 vs raw H3 (h3/night/*.mp4), never Wan."
